  {
    "id": 8756927692955,
    "title": "Chicken Pickle with Bone",
    "handle": "chicken-pickle-with-bone",
    "description": "For those who know — chicken on the bone always tastes better. The bone imparts a depth of flavour that boneless simply cannot match, and our Chicken Pickle with Bone delivers exactly that — rich, deeply flavoured, intensely spiced Andhra chicken pickle the traditional way. Chef Venkatesh follows the same recipe used in Andhra village kitchens for generations — fresh chicken pieces with bone, slow-cooked with bold spices, curry leaves and cold-pressed groundnut oil until every piece is completely infused with flavour. This is a pickle that serious non-veg lovers will not forget. Why our Chicken Pickle with Bone is different: Fresh chicken with bone — adds incredible depth of flavour Traditional Andhra village recipe Slow-cooked with freshly ground spices Cold-pressed groundnut oil — never",
    "html": "<p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]\">For those who know — chicken on the bone always tastes better. The bone imparts a depth of flavour that boneless simply cannot match, and our Chicken Pickle with Bone delivers exactly that — rich, deeply flavoured, intensely spiced Andhra chicken pickle the traditional way.</p>\n<p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]\">Chef Venkatesh follows the same recipe used in Andhra village kitchens for generations — fresh chicken pieces with bone, slow-cooked with bold spices, curry leaves and cold-pressed groundnut oil until every piece is completely infused with flavour. This is a pickle that serious non-veg lovers will not forget.</p>\n<p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]\"><strong>Why our Chicken Pickle with Bone is different:</strong></p>\n<ul class=\"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3\">\n<li class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\">Fresh chicken with bone — adds incredible depth of flavour</li>\n<li class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\">Traditional Andhra village recipe</li>\n<li class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\">Slow-cooked with freshly ground spices</li>\n<li class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\">Cold-pressed groundnut oil — never refined oil</li>\n<li class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\">Zero preservatives, FSSAI certified</li>\n<li class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\">Handcrafted in small batches</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]\"><strong>Best enjoyed with:</strong> Hot steamed rice and ghee, warm roti or chapati. A showstopper at any meal.</p>\n<p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]\"><strong>Storage:</strong> Store in a cool dry place. Always use a clean dry spoon. Refrigerate after opening. Consume within 3 months.</p>\n<p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]\"><em>Tip: The bone releases natural gelatin into the oil which makes the gravy richer over time — this pickle tastes even better after a few days.</em></p>",
